[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Variation "Hillbilly Attack, Schaeffer Gambit"]
[ECO "B10"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,early-queen"]
[Refutes "1. e4 c6 2. Bc4 d5 3. Bb3 dxe4 4. Qh5 g6 5. Qe5"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "for-us"]
[Opponent "4.Qh5"]
[Start "1. e4 c6 2. Bc4 d5 3. Bb3 dxe4"]

4. Qh5 { The queen and bishop both aim at f7, so White threatens Qxf7 mate. } 4... g6 { Attacks the queen with a pawn and blocks the h5 to f7 diagonal. } 5. Qe5 $2 { Threatens the rook on h8, but the queen is now far from the rest of White's army. } 5... Nf6 { Blocks the attack on h8, develops, and leaves White's queen offside. Black is a pawn up with an easy game. } 6. Nc3 Bf5 *
